<article class="env-lemma" id="02WT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02WT">Lemma <span data-tag="02WT">65.10.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $U$ be a scheme over $S$. Let $j = (s, t) : R \to U \times _ S U$ be an étale equivalence relation on $U$ over $S$. Let $U' \to U$ be an étale morphism. Let $R'$ be the restriction of $R$ to $U'$, see Groupoids, Definition <a href="/tag/02V9" data-tag="02V9">39.3.3</a>. Then $j' : R' \to U' \times _ S U'$ is an étale equivalence relation also. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is clear from the description of $s', t'$ in Groupoids, Lemma <a href="/tag/02VB" data-tag="02VB">39.18.1</a> that $s' , t' : R' \to U'$ are étale as compositions of base changes of étale morphisms (see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02GO" data-tag="02GO">29.37.4</a> and <a href="/tag/02GN" data-tag="02GN">29.37.3</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>